viousAdminRole` `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` is the starting admin for all roles, despite {RoleAdminChanged} not being emitted signaling this."},"RoleGranted(bytes32,address,address)":{"details":"Emitted when `account` is granted `role`. `sender` is the account that originated the contract call, an admin role bearer except when using {AccessControl-_setupRole}."},"RoleRevoked(bytes32,address,address)":{"details":"Emitted when `account` is revoked `role`. `sender` is the account that originated the contract call:   - if using `revokeRole`, it is the admin role bearer   - if using `renounceRole`, it is the role bearer (i.e. `account`)"},"ThreePoAdapter__QuestionInitialized(bytes32,bytes32,address)":{"params":{"questionID":"- The UMA CTF adapter question ID.","threePoID":"- The 3Po protocol question identifier.","umaCompatibleCtfAdapter":"- The UMA-compatible CTF adapter address."}},"ThreePoAdapter__QuestionResolved(bytes32,bytes32,uint256)":{"params":{"outcomeValueScaled":"- The scaled outcome value proposed.","questionID":"- The UMA CTF adapter question ID.","threePoID":"- The 3Po protocol question identifier."}},"ThreePoAdapter__SignerUpdated(address,bool)":{"params":{"isWhitelisted":"- Whether the signer is whitelisted.","signer":"- The signer address."}},"ThreePoAdapter__UmaCompatibleCtfAdaptersWhitelisted(address[],bool)":{"params":{"isWhitelisted":"- Whether the UMA-compatible CTF adapters are whitelisted.","umaCompatibleCtfAdapters":"- The UMA-compatible CTF adapter addresses."}}},"kind":"dev","methods":{"constructor":{"params":{"_admin":"- Address of the admin.","_optimisticOracle":"- Address of the UMA-compatible Optimistic Oracle."}},"getRoleAdmin(bytes32)":{"details":"Returns the admin role that controls `role`. See {grantRole} and {revokeRole}. To change a role's admin, use {_setRoleAdmin}."},"grantRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Grants `role` to `account`. If `account` had not been already granted `role`, emits a {RoleGranted} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role. May emit a {RoleGranted} event."},"hasRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Returns `true` if `account` has been granted `role`."},"initialize(address,bytes,bytes32)":{"details":"Calls the CTF adapter's initialize with fixed params (dead reward token, zero reward/bond/liveness). Initializer only.","params":{"ancillaryData":"- Data used to resolve the condition in the CTF adapter.","threePoID":"- The 3Po protocol question identifier to associate with the new internal question."}},"renounceRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from the calling account. Roles are often managed via {grantRole} and {revokeRole}: this function's purpose is to provide a mechanism for accounts to lose their privileges if they are compromised (such as when a trusted device is misplaced). If the calling account had been revoked `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must be `callerConfirmation`. May emit a {RoleRevoked} event."},"resolve(bytes32,uint256,bytes)":{"details":"Reverts if the 3Po ID is unknown or the signature is from a non-whitelisted signer.","params":{"outcomeValueScaled":"- The scaled outcome value to propose (e.g. 0, 0.5 or 1 for binary).","signature":"- ECDSA signature from a whitelisted signer over (threePoID, outcomeValueScaled).","threePoID":"- The 3Po protocol question identifier."}},"revokeRole(bytes32,address)":{"details":"Revokes `role` from `account`. If `account` had been granted `role`, emits a {RoleRevoked} event. Requirements: - the caller must have ``role``'s admin role. May emit a {RoleRevoked} event."},"supportsInterface(bytes4)":{"details":"See {IERC165-supportsInterface}."},"updateIsUmaCompatibleCtfAdapterWhitelisted(address[],bool)":{"params":{"isWhitelisted":"- Whether the UMA-compatible CTF adapters are whitelisted.","umaCompatibleCtfAdapters":"- The UMA-compatible CTF adapter addresses to update."}},"updateSigner(address,bool)":{"params":{"isWhitelisted":"- True to allow this signer's si